    // ── end front 36 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    // ── front 37 — flexbox, grid and gap ─────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // `Flex` is the flex CONTAINER and the flex ITEM: direction and wrap, the
    // `flex` shorthand, grow, shrink, basis and order. `display:flex` is NOT
    // here — it is a display value and front 36's; this section is what a box
    // that already declares it can say next.
    //
    // The shorthand's sub-section is `Value` and not `Flex`, because a section
    // cannot carry a sub-section of its own name.
    //
    // `Basis` is the one family here that is a LENGTH, and it answers front
    // 54's `spacing(n)` / `spacingHalf(n)` over front 35's scale, so
    // `.Flex.Basis.4` and `.Pad.All.4` carry the same length text BY
    // CONSTRUCTION. `Grow`, `Shrink` and `Order` are bare numbers and reach
    // `spacing` never: `order-1` is `order:1`, and `order-first` is the
    // sentinel `-9999`, not a keyword.
    Flex {
        Row,
        RowReverse,
        Col,
        ColReverse,
        Wrap,
        WrapReverse,
        NoWrap,
        Value {
            One,
            Auto,
            Initial,
            None,
        }
        Grow {
            0,
            1,
        }
        Shrink {
            0,
            1,
        }
        Basis {
            0,
