    // `Grid` is the two-dimensional half of `§ 6` — templates, spans, starts,
    // ends, auto-flow and the implicit tracks. `display:grid` is front 36's;
    // before this section there was nothing to put inside the box it declares.
    //
    // NOTHING HERE IS A LENGTH. A column count, a span and a line number are
    // integers, so no leaf reaches `spacing` and no leaf spells a `rem`; the
    // one composed value, `repeat(N, minmax(0, 1fr))`, is built by `gridRepeat`
    // from the leaf's numeral and is spelled in exactly one place.
    //
    // `Start` and `End` run to 13 because a twelve-column grid has THIRTEEN
    // LINES. `Cols`/`Rows` and `Span` run to 12.
